  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Non-inverting amplifier and voltage follower"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "In the non-inverting amplifier the input goes to the + terminal, and $R_f$ with $R_1$ (to ground) feed back a fraction $R_1/(R_1+R_f)$ of the output to the − terminal. Since $V_- \\approx V_+ = V_i$, $V_o = V_i(1 + R_f/R_1)$, so $A_v = 1 + R_f/R_1$, in phase, with a very high input resistance. With $R_f = 0$ and $R_1$ removed, $A_v = 1$: the voltage follower, a buffer with very high input and very low output resistance. In practice the output is limited to about ±13 V with a ±15 V supply (saturation)."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Av = 1 + Rf/R1, in phase"
    },
    {
     "en": "Very high input resistance"
    },
    {
     "en": "Voltage follower: Av = 1, buffer"
    },
    {
     "en": "Output saturates near ±(VCC − 2 V)"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "For the non-inverting amplifier the gain is one plus Rf over R1, in phase. The voltage follower has a gain of exactly one and is used as a buffer.",
    "kn": "ನಾನ್-ಇನ್ವರ್ಟಿಂಗ್ ವರ್ಧಕದ ವರ್ಧನೆ 1 + Rf/R1, ಒಂದೇ ಹಂತದಲ್ಲಿ. ವೋಲ್ಟೇಜ್ ಫಾಲೋವರ್‌ನ ವರ್ಧನೆ 1; ಅದನ್ನು ಬಫರ್ ಆಗಿ ಬಳಸುತ್ತಾರೆ."
   },
   "formula": "A_v = 1 + \\frac{R_f}{R_1}"
  },
